{"content":[{"c":["ELIAKIM"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Hilkiah’s son and a royal officer in the household and court of King Hezekiah (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.18.18,26,37","r":"2Kgs.18.18,26,37","rawR":"2Kgs.18.18,26,37","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.18.18,26,37","value":"2Kgs.18.18,26,37"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 18:18, 26, 37"},"). His position had increased in importance since Solomon’s reign (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.4.2-6","r":"1Kgs.4.2-6","rawR":"1Kgs.4.2-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.4.2-6","value":"1Kgs.4.2-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 4:2-6"},") until he was second only to the king. As such, Eliakim had absolute authority as the king’s representative."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["When Sennacherib of Assyria moved against Jerusalem in 701 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},", Eliakim was one of the diplomatic emissaries who conferred with the Assyrian officers on behalf of Hezekiah (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.18.18,26","r":"2Kgs.18.18,26","rawR":"2Kgs.18.18,26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.18.18,26","value":"2Kgs.18.18,26"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 18:18, 26"},"). He was also sent by Hezekiah in sackcloth to Isaiah to ask for prayer on Jerusalem’s behalf (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.19.1-5","r":"2Kgs.19.1-5","rawR":"2Kgs.19.1-5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.19.1-5","value":"2Kgs.19.1-5"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 19:1-5"},")."],"sourceClass":"list-text","t":"p"},{"c":["2. King Josiah’s second son. When Eliakim was made king of Judah by Pharaoh Neco, his name was changed to Jehoiakim (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.23.34","r":"2Kgs.23.34","rawR":"2Kgs.23.34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.23.34","value":"2Kgs.23.34"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 23:34"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.36.4","r":"2Chr.36.4","rawR":"2Chr.36.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.36.4","value":"2Chr.36.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 36:4"},"). ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Jehoiakim_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Jehoiakim_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Jehoiakim_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Jehoiakim"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. One of the priests who assisted at the dedication of the Jerusalem wall after it was rebuilt by Zerubbabel (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.41","r":"Neh.12.41","rawR":"Neh.12.41","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.41","value":"Neh.12.41"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:41"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Abiud’s son in Matthew’s genealogy of Jesus (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.1.13","r":"Matt.1.13","rawR":"Matt.1.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.1.13","value":"Matt.1.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 1:13"},"). ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Genealogy of Jesus Christ"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["5. Melea’s son in Luke’s genealogy of Jesus (",{"href":"?bref=Luke.3.30","r":"Luke.3.30","rawR":"Luke.3.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.3.30","value":"Luke.3.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 3:30"},"). ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Genealogy of Jesus Christ"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Eliakim","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 18:18, 26, 37","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.18.18,26,37","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.18.18,26,37","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.18.18,26,37"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 4:2-6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.4.2-6","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.4.2-6","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.4.2-6"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 18:18, 26","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.18.18,26","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.18.18,26","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.18.18,26"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 19:1-5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.19.1-5","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.19.1-5","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.19.1-5"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 23:34","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.23.34","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.23.34","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.23.34"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 36:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.36.4","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.36.4","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.36.4"},{"anchorText":"Neh 12:41","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.12.41","rawQueryValue":"Neh.12.41","sourceRefExact":"Neh.12.41"},{"anchorText":"Mt 1:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.1.13","rawQueryValue":"Matt.1.13","sourceRefExact":"Matt.1.13"},{"anchorText":"Lk 3:30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.3.30","rawQueryValue":"Luke.3.30","sourceRefExact":"Luke.3.30"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"5586146a312ef0ffc568db1d28a44edfd789621e9f9a5db7eff034fe1410a42e","sourceItemName":"Eliakim","sourceItemOrder":88,"sourceMember":"Articles/E.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Eliakim","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Eliakim","title":"Eliakim","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}